WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.640
Speaker 1: I often get emails that say, David,&nbsp;
is the modern Republican Party now fascist? Is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:16.200
fascism what they would employ if there were no&nbsp;
barriers or opposition or obstacles? So let's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:22.380
explore this a little bit and think it through.&nbsp;
And where I end up coming down is that the modern&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:31.200
Republican Party is a fascistic, authoritarian&nbsp;
party, but not actually fascist. But part of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:36.120
the reason why they are not actually fascist is&nbsp;
that there is opposition in the United States.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:40.380
So let's start with the definition. What are&nbsp;
we talking about when we talk about fascism?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:49.320
Fascism is a far right authoritarian political&nbsp;
ideology which often includes dictatorial power,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:58.260
forcible suppression of opposition and&nbsp;
very strongly regimented society and a very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:04.800
strongly regimented economy. Now, some of these&nbsp;
things might not sound like the rhetoric of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:09.360
Republican Party. What strong regimentation the&nbsp;
Republican Party is all about Freedom and liberty.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:14.280
Yes, the rhetoric is. But are they actually like&nbsp;
that when it comes to policy? So we're going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:21.780
talk about that. What is the Republican Party&nbsp;
platform and policy versus fascism or fascistic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:29.400
authoritarianism? Because it is true that it used&nbsp;
to be the case that the Republican Party was known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:37.140
for conservative values, actually being for small&nbsp;
government, promoting truly free market capitalism&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:42.360
or something close to it. But that is not at&nbsp;
all what the modern modern Republican Party,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:48.780
particularly under MAGA Trumpism, has become.&nbsp;
It has become a party of hyper nationalism,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:58.140
populist rhetoric, as well as extraordinarily&nbsp;
overbearing suppression of opposition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:05.520
all fascistic characteristics. And the&nbsp;
bulk of this, the culmination of it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:11.100
has been seen in the shift during the rise&nbsp;
of Donald Trump and his influence on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:16.560
Republican Party. The rhetoric of Trump and&nbsp;
the policies that Trumpists would like to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:25.200
implement are every combination of authoritarian,&nbsp;
sometimes xenophobic, anti-competitive, etc. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:30.000
we're going to look at a bunch of examples the&nbsp;
Muslim ban, family separation at the border,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.640
trying to overturn the 2020 presidential election&nbsp;
results, trying to limit the speech of the press&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:42.840
and trying to get adversarial reporters banned,&nbsp;
including Jim Acosta, etc.. In addition to this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:48.529
the attempt to suppress opposition.
Speaker 2: Through.&nbsp;

00:02:48.529 --> 00:02:53.880
Speaker 1: Election meddling tactics that&nbsp;
disproportionately affect young people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:58.320
people of color, low income individuals,&nbsp;
disproportionately, those who vote on the left is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:05.160
another way in which Republicans under MAGA have&nbsp;
tried to hold on to power by any means necessary,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:11.280
even when they've been voted out completely anti&nbsp;
democratically. Now there are people who will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:20.700
argue these are straight up fascist tactics.&nbsp;
Others say it's kind of too extreme a term,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:27.900
but it is very hard to argue that it isn't&nbsp;
fascistic and hardline authoritarianism. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:34.800
actions and the rhetoric of MAGA Trumpism, a.k.a&nbsp;
the modern Republican Party have taken that bent.

